## Step 3: Apply Computational Thinking Skills
| **Sub-problem** | **CT Skill* | **Proposed Solution** |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Students take too long to decide what to order, causing delays and longer queues. |Abstraction | Display basic menu showcasing the available food, prices, and simple description to quicken students' decision process. |
| Slow and error-prone payment process. | Algorithm Design | Develop a step-by-step payment system that calculates the total cost, processes the payment, and provides the correct change. |
| Lack of real-time food inventory tracker | Pattern Recognition | Monitor food item quantity, and give out warning when stock reaches a low level. |
| The service process lacks proper organization | Decomposition | Divide the process into separate ordering, payment, and pickup stages to create a more organized flow for students. | 

